  data:  # d3dc
    kind: invariant  # d3dc
    title: "The SCIP importer's DescriptorKind map mints four unregistered Symbol.kind values (parameter, type_parameter, meta, unknown)"  # d3dc
    status: violated  # d3dc
    priority: 3  # d3dc
    parent:  # d3dc
    tags:  # d3dc
    - axis  # d3dc
    - symbol_kind  # d3dc
    - architecture  # d3dc
    - rust  # d3dc
    isbefore: []  # d3dc
    duplicate_of: []  # d3dc
    not_duplicate_of: []  # d3dc
    pr_ref:  # d3dc
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-01 by WI-jinuj's widening of axis_drift, on its FIRST run over\nthe live tree. This is the shape the widening exists to catch and could not\nsee before: the consumer is a DICT, and the collector read only sets.\n\nTHE FACT. scip/index.py:94 maps SCIP DescriptorKind -> Symbol.kind:\n\n    _KIND_MAP: Dict[DescriptorKind, str] = {\n        DescriptorKind.NAMESPACE:      \"namespace\",       IN registry\n        DescriptorKind.TYPE:           \"class\",           IN registry\n        DescriptorKind.TERM:           \"variable\",        IN registry\n        DescriptorKind.METHOD:         \"method\",          IN registry\n        DescriptorKind.MACRO:          \"macro\",           IN registry\n        DescriptorKind.TYPE_PARAMETER: \"type_parameter\",  *** ABSENT ***\n        DescriptorKind.PARAMETER:      \"parameter\",       *** ABSENT ***\n        DescriptorKind.META:           \"meta\",            *** ABSENT ***\n    }\n\nand index.py:166 reads it as `_KIND_MAP.get(last.kind, \"unknown\")` -- so a\nFOURTH unregistered value, \"unknown\", is minted whenever a descriptor kind is\nabsent from the map.\n\nWHY THIS IS NOT AN AXIS-NAME COLLISION, which is the usual explanation for a\nKIND-filtered offender and is the first thing to rule out: FIVE OF THE EIGHT\nVALUES ARE REGISTERED Symbol.kind names. A constant that is 5/8 conformant is\na consumer of this axis, not a different vocabulary that happens to match the\nsubstring filter. Contrast the constants excluded alongside it --\n_ANNOTATION_KINDS (arrow, rect), _PROVENANCE_KINDS (io_primitives, taint_*),\n_RELATED_ENDPOINT_KINDS (a meta[\"framework_role\"] vocabulary) -- each of which\nis 0/N conformant.\n\nEXPOSURE: the rust-analyzer / SCIP backend only (hypergumbo --backend\nrust-analyzer, and any other SCIP index ingested through this path). The\ndefault tree-sitter backend does not reach this code, which is why the\nphantom kinds have not surfaced in tree-sitter dogfooding.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: a Symbol carrying kind=\"parameter\" / \"type_parameter\" / \"meta\" /\n\"unknown\" is emitted into the behavior map with a kind no canonical registry\nentry describes, so every consumer that branches on Symbol.kind -- the\nADR-0027 axis classification, kind-keyed stable-id factories\n(analyze/base.py:1467 _KIND_STABLE_ID_FACTORIES), the noise-kind filter in\ncli.py -- meets a value it has no case for. NOT MEASURED: whether these\nkinds actually appear in output on a real SCIP index, or whether the\ndescriptor kinds that produce them are filtered upstream. DO THAT FIRST.\n\nWHY IT IS PARKED RATHER THAN FIXED HERE: WI-jinuj is the shared-machinery\nwidening, and its own scope says the per-axis residue wants FILING, not\nfixing, because a widening that turns four green linters red on landing is a\nbad landing. The exclusion carrying this item's id in symbol_kinds.py is\nDEBT, deliberately spelled differently from the collision exclusions beside\nit, and is the thing to delete when this closes.\n\nFIRST STEP: run the SCIP backend over a rust repo and count Symbols emitted\nwith each of the four values. If they are reachable, the fix is an ADR-0027\nregistry decision (are `parameter` / `type_parameter` legitimate\nlanguage-construct kinds -- Cluster A -- or should the SCIP importer fold\nthem to an existing kind?); \"unknown\" is separately a sentinel and per\nADR-0051's precedent a sentinel is NOT a conformant value of a construct\naxis. If they are unreachable, the map rows are dead and should be dropped."  # d3dc
    fields:  # d3dc
      statement: "scip/index.py:94 _KIND_MAP maps SCIP DescriptorKind to Symbol.kind. Five of its eight values are in the canonical symbol-kind registry (namespace, class, variable, method, macro) and three are NOT (type_parameter, parameter, meta); index.py:166 reads the map as _KIND_MAP.get(last.kind, 'unknown'), minting a fourth unregistered value. A Symbol emitted through the SCIP/rust-analyzer backend can therefore carry a kind that no canonical registry entry describes, which every ADR-0027 consumer that branches on Symbol.kind has no case for."  # d3dc
      root_cause: "The map is a DICT, and axis_drift's collector read only string-literal SETS, so no symbol-kind drift linter could ever see it (WI-jinuj). It is not an axis-name collision -- 5 of 8 values ARE registered symbol kinds, where the constants excluded alongside it are 0/N conformant. Whether the phantom values are REACHABLE in real SCIP output is NOT measured and is the filed first step."  # d3dc
